# Testing Regression Models

<img src="https://images.code.org/304b487ecbc79fe5221114de0cffba66-image-1794512083855.png" alt="A scatter plot of test data points with two fitted lines: Dani's model (dashed) and Sasha's model (solid), showing Dani's line passing exactly through some points while Sasha's line stays consistently close to all of them" style="width: 320px; border-radius: 10px; float: right; margin: 0 0 10px 20px;">

Lesson 6 opens with a debate: Dani and Sasha each built a regression model for the same test data. 

Dani's model gets more predictions exactly correct. Sasha's model never hits exactly, but every prediction stays close. Whose model is actually better?

